Tooth disease type 2A1 (CMT2A1) is a form of axonal Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease, a peripheral sensorimotor neuropathy. CMT2A presents with a more prominent muscle weakness in lower than upper limbs and frequent postural tremor.\" [Orphanet:99946]\nsubset: clingen {source=\"MONDO:CLINGEN\"}\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0110154\"}\nsubset: doid_rare {source=\"DOID:0110154\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0001248\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C150609\", source=\"NCIT:C134952\"}\nsubset: nord_rare {source=\"MONDO:NORD\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:118210\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:99946\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:99946\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:99946\"}\nsubset: otar {source=\"MONDO:OTAR\"}\nsubset: prototype_pattern\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"autosomal dominant Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 2A1\" RELATED []\nsynonym: \"Charcot Marie Tooth disease type 2A\" RELATED [GARD:0001248]\nsynonym: \"Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 2 caused by mutation in KIF1B\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern]\nsynonym: \"Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 2A\" EXACT [NCIT:C134952]\nsynonym: \"Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 2A1\" EXACT [DOID:0110154, icd11.foundation:2087067372, NCIT:C150609] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease, axonal, autosomal dominant, type 2A1\" RELATED []\nsynonym: \"Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease, axonal, type 2A\" RELATED [GARD:0001248]\nsynonym: \"Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease, axonal, type 2A1\" RELATED [MONDO:Lexical]\nsynonym: \"Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease, neuronal, type 2A\" RELATED [GARD:0001248]\nsynonym: \"Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease, neuronal, type 2A1\" RELATED []\nsynonym: \"Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease, type 2A1\" EXACT []\nsynonym: \"Charcot-Marie-Tooth neuropathy, type 2A1\" RELATED []\nsynonym: \"CMT 2A\" RELATED [GARD:0001248]\nsynonym: \"CMT2A\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [NCIT:C134952]\nsynonym: \"CMT2A1\" EXA